ion and holding $5.7 million on hand, while Republican Mike LiPetri has raised about $1.7 million with $725,000 available. No public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on expert ratings and market pricing.\n\nMost raters place the race in the Lean D to Likely D range, and prediction markets give Suozzi roughly a 91-92% chance of winning. Republicans are investing heavily: a Trump-linked super PAC has put about $8 million into ads attacking Suozzi over stock trading, and local coverage highlights GOP turnout efforts in Nassau County. Suozzi has responded with ads emphasizing his opposition to extremism, positioning himself as a moderate in a competitive district.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9133, "margin": 9.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.894, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8981, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.907, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8709, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8973, "margin": 9.5}]}